{
  "id": "ss.base.stump",
  "name": "Cut spire",
  "description": "A pheromone spire cut off flat. The signal has gone out of it: the trunk is a drained mauve rather than the field's pink, faceted the way a crystal grows, with chips at its foot. The face is pale and ringed like a tree, one ring per passing of the vermin (A030), with a little pink left at the heart and the saw's line across it. Three of these stand by the camp's south path, the cut spires the records found south of base (T010). In feelers they mark the way out to the Plains.",
